From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: max17042: MAX77705 full capacity is FullCapRep

The MAX77705's fuel gauge is driven as a MAX17047, which reports the
full capacity from 0x10 and calls the battery full when RepCap comes
within the threshold of it. On the MAX77705, RepSOC is RepCap over
FullCapRep at 0x35 (Samsung's FULLCAP_REP_REG; its reset path writes
RepCap and FullCapRep together), and 0x10 holds a smaller learned
capacity: on the Galaxy Z Flip3 RepCap 1017, RepSOC 95.6 %, 0x35 1064
(1017 / 1064 = 95.6 %) and 0x10 992. The battery read Full from about
93 % while still charging, and Plasma showed it as fully charged. Use
0x35 for the full capacity and the full test on the MAX77705.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c |   15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)


diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
index 505a68c..35504a2 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/max17042_battery.c
@@ -78,6 +78,7 @@ struct max17042_chip {
 	struct regmap *regmap;
 	struct power_supply *battery;
 	enum max170xx_chip_type chip_type;
+	unsigned int fullcap_reg;	/* the full capacity RepSOC is based on */
 	struct max17042_config_data *config_data;
 	struct delayed_work work;
 	int    irq;
@@ -168,7 +169,7 @@ static int max17042_get_status(struct max17042_chip *chip, int *status)
 	 * 2 to differ a bit.
 	 */
 
-	ret = regmap_read(chip->regmap, MAX17042_FullCAP, &charge_full);
+	ret = regmap_read(chip->regmap, chip->fullcap_reg, &charge_full);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
@@ -368,7 +369,7 @@ static int max17042_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 		val->intval = data64;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL:
-		ret = regmap_read(map, MAX17042_FullCAP, &data);
+		ret = regmap_read(map, chip->fullcap_reg, &data);
 		if (ret < 0)
 			return ret;
 
@@ -1451,6 +1452,16 @@ static int max17042_probe(struct i2c_client *client, struct device *dev, int irq
 	chip->dev = dev;
 	chip->chip_type = chip_type;
 
+	/*
+	 * The MAX77705's gauge reports its SOC against FullCapRep at 0x35
+	 * (Samsung's FULLCAP_REP_REG): RepSOC is RepCap / FullCapRep. 0x10
+	 * holds a smaller learned capacity there, so taking it as the full
+	 * capacity made the battery read Full from about 93 %.
+	 */
+	chip->fullcap_reg = MAX17042_FullCAP;
+	if (device_is_compatible(dev, "maxim,max77705-battery"))
+		chip->fullcap_reg = MAX17042_FullCAP0;
+
 	if (chip->chip_type == MAXIM_DEVICE_TYPE_MAX77759)
 		regmap_config = &max77759_fg_regmap_cfg;
 	else
